startPage 5 'What persists and what is a mockup?' 'Use database-backed CSV for real stock maintenance.';$y=section 132 'IMPORT BEHAVIOR';$y=para 42 $y 'The complete CSV is validated in a database transaction. A failure rolls back the file. A successful import inserts or updates the tenant + plant + material record. A repeat upload replaces that that pair quantities; it does not append history. It cannot create missing plants or materials. Database quantities support four decimal places.' 500 8.5 '#475D78' 12;$y+=8;$y=section $y 'ADD INVENTORY FORM';$y=para 42 $y 'The form displays material code/name/type/category/unit/description, opening/min/max/safety stock, supplier/preferred supplier, price/currency, storage/shelf, lead time, and minimum order quantity. These are design fields only: submit adds a temporary browser row; Save as Draft only notifies. Use CSV for persisted changes.' 500 8.3 '#475D78' 12;$y+=8;$y=section $y 'DETAIL MODAL AND TABS';$rows=@(@('Overview / Stock Details','Some values are API-backed. Safety Stock 100 Kg, Opening Stock 200 Kg, Last Issue Date are hard-coded examples.'),@('Stock Transactions / Recent Transactions','No transaction endpoint; movement list is empty.'),@('Suppliers, Purchase History, Usage History, Related Materials','Placeholder tabs; no detail data is loaded.'),@('Stock Movement chart','Static illustrative six-month bars, not actual receipts/issues.'),@('Status / Reorder Required / Lead Time','Status API-derived; reorder compares on-hand with min; lead time fixed at 10 days.'),@('Edit / View All / row actions','Notification-only, no database write or history retrieval.'));foreach($r in $rows){$y=item $y $r[0] $r[1]};$y+=6;[void](para 42 $y 'The "Last Receipt Date" column is currently an inbound ETA field. Read it as transit due date in this release.' 500 8 '#95600E' 11 $true);endPage

# Page 6
startPage 6 'How inventory changes the MRP plan' 'Use the bucket timing and quantity rules to validate a simple case by hand.';$y=section 132 'CONCEPTUAL BUCKET FLOW';$steps=@('Start from on_hand_qty','Add scheduled receipt in first bucket','Add transit in due-date bucket (blank = first bucket)','Consume gross material need','Compare projected stock to effective minimum','Recommend net order; apply MOQ, multiple, lead time','Flag capacity excess');$i=1;foreach($s in $steps){txt 48 $y ("{0}." -f $i) 8 '#1679E8' $true;$y=para 69 $y $s 470 8.5 '#475D78' 12;$y+=4;$i++};$y+=4;$y=section $y 'IMPORTANT CALCULATION BOUNDARIES';$rows=@(@('Reserved quantity','Imported and shown but current forward MRP starts with on-hand and does not subtract reserved.'),@('Scheduled receipts','One undated CSV total; assumed available in first bucket.'),@('Transit due date','Selects receipt bucket; empty means first bucket.'),@('Reorder level','Different from min stock; not part of current forward netting.'),@('Capacity','Can create an alert; it does not cap the order quantity.'),@('Inventory value','Estimate from quantity x unit cost, not financial ledger valuation.'));foreach($r in $rows){$y=item $y $r[0] $r[1]};$y+=6;$y=section $y 'OPERATOR CHECKLIST';[void](para 42 $y '1. Verify tenant.  2. Upload plant/material masters and optional constraints.  3. Check units and plant/material codes.  4. Upload exact CSV headers.  5. Confirm success row count.  6. Compare list values with CSV and precedence rules.  7. Run a matching MRP scenario and inspect opening stock and receipt buckets.  8. Reconcile gross need and the safety-stock gap manually.' 500 7.7 '#475D78' 11);endPage

